# TRUST — the keys this label accepts grants and scores from.
#
# One key per line:   ed25519:<base64>   <who they are>   [# note]
#
# There is no certificate authority here and no registry to phone. A key is
# trusted because a human read a pull request and merged it, and `git blame`
# on this file says who, when, and in which commit. That is a smaller and more
# honest trust model than any PKI: the question "why does the label accept
# this person's grants?" always has an answer, and the answer is a link.
#
# To join:  python3 signing.py keygen --out keys/you --name "Your Name"
#           add the printed ed25519: line below, open a pull request.
#
# To leave, or after a compromise: delete the line. Everything that key ever
# signed stops verifying on the next CI run — which is the point of checking
# grants at verification time rather than baking a decision into a file once.

